WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.302
[music playing]

00:00:02.368 --> 00:00:04.604
 James, Paul, congratulations.

00:00:04.671 --> 00:00:06.539
You guys have made it to
the third and final round

00:00:06.606 --> 00:00:07.941
of this competition.

00:00:08.008 --> 00:00:09.575
Now, when you came here,
we threw a little twisted

00:00:09.642 --> 00:00:10.977
Damascus challenge at you.

00:00:11.077 --> 00:00:12.812
Now we're sending you
back to your home forges

00:00:12.912 --> 00:00:15.814
to recreate this iconic
weapon from history.

00:00:15.915 --> 00:00:16.715
Ready to see it?

00:00:16.782 --> 00:00:17.516
 Yeah.

00:00:17.583 --> 00:00:18.317
 Sure.

00:00:18.384 --> 00:00:20.420
 All right, that weapon is--

00:00:24.023 --> 00:00:25.558
the darb sri gun chai.

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:28.394
 I have never seen
anything like this.

00:00:28.494 --> 00:00:30.729
I can't even pronounce
the name of this thing.

00:00:30.796 --> 00:00:31.964
"Doob-tree goo-trabi?"

00:00:32.031 --> 00:00:33.732
What did he say?

00:00:33.799 --> 00:00:34.700
 Good luck, gentlemen.

00:00:34.767 --> 00:00:35.968
We'll see you in four days.

00:00:36.069 --> 00:00:36.969
 Good luck, man.

00:00:37.036 --> 00:00:38.837 line:14%
 Good luck.

00:00:38.938 --> 00:00:41.808 line:14%
[music playing]

00:00:41.875 --> 00:00:44.910
 Day one, I'm ready
to get hammering.

00:00:45.010 --> 00:00:46.679
I'm going to be using 80CrV2.

00:00:46.779 --> 00:00:50.349
It's a very good steel for
impact and edge retention.

00:00:50.449 --> 00:00:51.617
And I believe the
tests that they're

00:00:51.684 --> 00:00:53.052
going to be putting
this blade through,

00:00:53.119 --> 00:00:54.353
it's going to need a
little bit of both.

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:55.989
This is a big chunk
of steel, so it's

00:00:56.056 --> 00:00:57.257
going to take a minute to
get the tip forged down

00:00:57.323 --> 00:00:58.657
to where I want it
before I can start

00:00:58.757 --> 00:00:59.959
drawing it out to the length.

00:01:00.026 --> 00:01:01.127
[music playing]

00:01:01.227 --> 00:01:02.729
The thing I'm
struggling with the most

00:01:02.796 --> 00:01:05.031
is the weight of
this entire blade.

00:01:05.131 --> 00:01:06.699
I'm having trouble keeping
this thing straight

00:01:06.799 --> 00:01:08.033
when I take it out of the forge.

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:09.469
It's the end of day one.

00:01:09.535 --> 00:01:12.138
Pretty happy with the
progress-- got it all drawn out.

00:01:12.204 --> 00:01:13.940
I'm ready for a bath, and
get started on this thing

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:15.742 line:14%
first thing in the morning.

00:01:15.809 --> 00:01:18.844 line:14%
[music playing]

00:01:18.911 --> 00:01:21.513
PAUL: It's day one here at my
shop in Fairfield, Connecticut.

00:01:21.580 --> 00:01:24.084
And I'm going to be making
a darb sri gun chai.

00:01:25.484 --> 00:01:27.019
For this challenge, I'm going
to be making ladder pattern

00:01:27.119 --> 00:01:28.721
Damascus, because it's
really going to set

00:01:28.787 --> 00:01:30.123
me apart from the competition.

00:01:30.189 --> 00:01:32.625
This is 15N20, that's the 1084.

00:01:32.691 --> 00:01:34.994
I got to make sure there's
no grease or oil on them,

00:01:35.094 --> 00:01:37.096
because that could
affect the forge weld.

00:01:37.163 --> 00:01:38.397
After I get the
steel cleaned up,

00:01:38.498 --> 00:01:40.799
I stack all the
pieces up together

00:01:40.866 --> 00:01:44.704
and do my initial weld.

00:01:44.771 --> 00:01:46.873
I'm feeling really good
that the welds have stock.

00:01:46.939 --> 00:01:50.075
That's one of the most difficult
parts of the entire process.

00:01:50.142 --> 00:01:53.112
The next step is to grind
in notches all along

00:01:53.212 --> 00:01:55.181
the entire thing on both sides.

00:01:55.281 --> 00:01:57.249
And what that's
going to do is expose

00:01:57.349 --> 00:01:59.052
the layers of the Damascus.

00:01:59.152 --> 00:02:01.421
It's the end of day one,
and I'm in pretty good shape

00:02:01.487 --> 00:02:03.890
for the rest of the challenge.

00:02:03.957 --> 00:02:05.224 line:14%
[music playing]

00:02:05.291 --> 00:02:06.625 line:14%
 Pretty nervous today--

00:02:06.692 --> 00:02:08.595 line:8%
we're going to do this
heat treat this morning.

00:02:08.661 --> 00:02:10.530
I'm only halfway
through with the time.

00:02:10.596 --> 00:02:13.065
So hopefully, if
something does happen,

00:02:13.132 --> 00:02:15.301
I've got time to
make another one.

00:02:15.368 --> 00:02:19.972
Look at that-- four leaf
clover, right at my feet.

00:02:20.039 --> 00:02:21.040
I hope it's a good sign.

00:02:21.107 --> 00:02:24.677
[music playing]

00:02:31.316 --> 00:02:33.720
I didn't feel any pings or pops.

00:02:33.820 --> 00:02:35.954
I'm happy.

00:02:36.055 --> 00:02:37.590
[music playing]

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:40.092
 It's the last day,
and it's about time

00:02:40.159 --> 00:02:42.228
to start etching the blade.

00:02:42.295 --> 00:02:45.498
This is the most magical
moment of making Damascus,

00:02:45.565 --> 00:02:47.767
because you get to finally
see what the pattern's

00:02:47.867 --> 00:02:48.934
going to look like.

00:02:49.035 --> 00:02:51.671
I'm still getting
streaks, though.

00:02:51.738 --> 00:02:53.473
I don't get it.

00:02:53.539 --> 00:02:56.276
It's just not at all
what I wanted to see.

00:02:56.342 --> 00:02:59.846 line:8%
There's a bunch of decarb all
over the entire blade, which

00:02:59.913 --> 00:03:01.547 line:8%
means I didn't
grind deep enough,

00:03:01.613 --> 00:03:03.983 line:8%
and the etch is not
going to come out right.

00:03:04.083 --> 00:03:06.385
So I could either
leave the decarb,

00:03:06.452 --> 00:03:09.422
and the Damascus just
won't be as good-looking,

00:03:09.522 --> 00:03:11.257
or I could grind into
the blade a little bit

00:03:11.324 --> 00:03:13.092
and risk making
the blade too thin.

00:03:13.159 --> 00:03:14.360
[music playing]

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:16.029
I knew in order to
save the pattern,

00:03:16.095 --> 00:03:19.198
I really had to just
go back to the grinder.

00:03:19.298 --> 00:03:22.167
And I think it's pretty good.

00:03:22.234 --> 00:03:24.236
This is the Damascus
I wanted to see.

00:03:24.303 --> 00:03:27.306
I'm still kind of
concerned that the blade is

00:03:27.372 --> 00:03:28.908
a little on the thinner side.

00:03:28.975 --> 00:03:31.743 line:8%
But there's nothing
I can do now.

00:03:31.844 --> 00:03:33.313 line:14%
[music playing]

00:03:33.413 --> 00:03:34.480 line:8%
JAMES: Here comes the light
at the end of the tunnel.

00:03:34.580 --> 00:03:36.182
So far, I've got the blade done.

00:03:36.282 --> 00:03:38.518
So I'm going to start
working on the handle.

00:03:38.584 --> 00:03:40.787
I don't have long enough
drill bits to drill

00:03:40.853 --> 00:03:42.155
all the way into that handle.

00:03:42.255 --> 00:03:43.990
So I'm going to have to
carve out a channel for that

00:03:44.057 --> 00:03:45.525
tang to sit in, and
make sure the wood

00:03:45.591 --> 00:03:47.626
marries back together nicely.

00:03:47.693 --> 00:03:49.295
Yeah, baby.

00:03:49.395 --> 00:03:51.396
Made it a little of my
own by adding some fur

00:03:51.496 --> 00:03:53.399
from the land around my house.

00:03:53.466 --> 00:03:55.400
I think that's going to
add a little special touch.

00:03:55.501 --> 00:03:56.969
It is a little on
the heavy side,

00:03:57.069 --> 00:03:58.104
but it's balanced perfectly.

00:03:58.171 --> 00:03:59.305
It's very wieldable.

00:03:59.372 --> 00:04:00.606
I'd say, yeah.

00:04:00.706 --> 00:04:03.709
All I can tell you is
grab it by the rabbit.

00:04:03.776 --> 00:04:06.545
 All right, bladesmiths,
welcome to the kill test.

00:04:06.645 --> 00:04:09.248
Your darb sri gun chais
look intimidating.

00:04:09.348 --> 00:04:10.582
But are they deadly?

00:04:10.682 --> 00:04:12.252
To find that out, I
will take your weapon,

00:04:12.318 --> 00:04:15.121
deliver some killing blows
to this ballistics dummy.

00:04:15.221 --> 00:04:15.988
James, you're up first.

00:04:16.055 --> 00:04:17.190
You ready for this?

00:04:17.256 --> 00:04:18.223
 There's nothing I
can do to stop it.

00:04:18.290 --> 00:04:19.191
 All right, let's do it.

00:04:19.258 --> 00:04:20.893
[music playing]

00:04:20.993 --> 00:04:23.595
 To say I'm nervous right
now is an understatement.

00:04:23.662 --> 00:04:25.531
At this point, it's
out of my hands.

00:04:25.631 --> 00:04:26.866
I just hope it can hold up.

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:34.474
[music playing]

00:04:43.249 --> 00:04:46.686
[music playing]

00:04:47.353 --> 00:04:48.287
 All right, James--

00:04:48.387 --> 00:04:50.390
first up, that's a beast.

00:04:50.490 --> 00:04:53.225
It's very forward heavy, so it
definitely feels like a chopper

00:04:53.292 --> 00:04:54.694
all the way through.

00:04:54.760 --> 00:04:58.231
Now, your handle here-- by
adding this fur around it,

00:04:58.298 --> 00:05:01.266
I can't get a good grip on
it because it's so soft.

00:05:01.333 --> 00:05:04.437
Now, your edge is sharp.

00:05:04.537 --> 00:05:07.239
Overall, sir, it'll kill.

00:05:07.306 --> 00:05:08.240
 Thank you.

00:05:08.307 --> 00:05:09.274
 All right, Paul, your turn.

00:05:09.374 --> 00:05:10.009
So are you ready?

00:05:10.109 --> 00:05:11.077
 I'm ready.

00:05:11.143 --> 00:05:12.344
DOUG MARCAIDA: Let's do this.

00:05:12.411 --> 00:05:14.647
PAUL: I built my blade
to be very light.

00:05:14.713 --> 00:05:17.049
It definitely makes me nervous
seeing the ballistics dummy,

00:05:17.116 --> 00:05:19.185
because I know there's a
lot of hard bones in there.

00:05:19.251 --> 00:05:21.454
And I'm definitely a little
bit worried that it could bend,

00:05:21.554 --> 00:05:22.654
even break in half.

00:05:22.754 --> 00:05:23.722
You never know what's
going to happen.

00:05:23.823 --> 00:05:27.060
[music playing]

00:05:28.061 --> 00:05:31.664
[music playing]

00:05:39.972 --> 00:05:43.308
[music playing]

00:05:43.408 --> 00:05:44.677
 All right, Paul--

00:05:44.777 --> 00:05:46.846
first up, I really appreciate
the Damascus pattern

00:05:46.913 --> 00:05:48.181
that you brought out here.

00:05:48.247 --> 00:05:50.650
Now, the fact that I
can hold the weapon out

00:05:50.717 --> 00:05:54.153
extended like this shows
just how light this weapon

00:05:54.220 --> 00:05:55.454
is for its size.

00:05:55.554 --> 00:05:57.690
And because of that, I
can cut deeply into this

00:05:57.790 --> 00:06:00.626
without using the weight,
just velocity alone.

00:06:00.693 --> 00:06:02.561
But after that strike
through the skull,

00:06:02.661 --> 00:06:04.429
it's picked up a
little bit of a bend.

00:06:04.496 --> 00:06:06.632
Overall, sir, it will kill.

00:06:06.699 --> 00:06:08.900
 Thank you.

00:06:09.001 --> 00:06:10.203
[music playing]

00:06:10.269 --> 00:06:11.437
 All right, gentlemen,
to test the strength

00:06:11.503 --> 00:06:13.072
and overall construction
of your blades,

00:06:13.139 --> 00:06:15.407
I'll be chopping
into these pots.

00:06:15.474 --> 00:06:16.909
Now, remember, this
is not about what

00:06:16.975 --> 00:06:19.077
your blades do to the
targets, but what the targets

00:06:19.144 --> 00:06:21.313
can do to your blades.

00:06:21.380 --> 00:06:22.148
James, you're up first.

00:06:22.215 --> 00:06:22.915
Are you ready?

00:06:22.982 --> 00:06:23.783
 Let it happen.

00:06:23.850 --> 00:06:24.650
DAVID BAKER: OK.

00:06:24.751 --> 00:06:28.121
[music playing]

00:06:33.025 --> 00:06:36.529
[music playing]

00:06:41.700 --> 00:06:42.468
 Phew.

00:06:45.171 --> 00:06:46.539
[music playing]

00:06:46.605 --> 00:06:49.374
 This is a
shoulder-ripping monster.

00:06:49.441 --> 00:06:52.344
Once you start this
thing moving, stopping it

00:06:52.411 --> 00:06:54.179
is really rough
on the shoulders.

00:06:54.279 --> 00:06:55.748
The fur around the middle here--

00:06:55.815 --> 00:06:58.617
it's a neat look, but
it's very slick, actually.

00:06:58.684 --> 00:07:02.955
And then your edge
is still sharp.

00:07:03.022 --> 00:07:03.823
You nailed it.

00:07:03.923 --> 00:07:04.390
Good job.

00:07:04.490 --> 00:07:05.625
 Thank you.

00:07:05.691 --> 00:07:06.525
DAVID BAKER: All
right, Paul, you're up.

00:07:06.625 --> 00:07:07.359
Are you ready?
- Yeah.

00:07:07.460 --> 00:07:08.194
DAVID BAKER: OK.

00:07:08.261 --> 00:07:09.528
[music playing]

00:07:09.595 --> 00:07:11.497
PAUL: I see the pots,
and I'm very worried.

00:07:11.564 --> 00:07:12.698
I feel like it
could bend my blade

00:07:12.798 --> 00:07:13.966
even more than it already is.

00:07:14.033 --> 00:07:16.102
If something goes wrong,
then I'm finished.

00:07:20.206 --> 00:07:23.776
[music playing]

00:07:28.480 --> 00:07:29.414
 (WHISPERING) Good job, dude.

00:07:29.481 --> 00:07:31.851
 (WHISPERING) Thanks.

00:07:31.917 --> 00:07:34.220
DAVID BAKER: All right,
Paul-- right off, this weapon

00:07:34.286 --> 00:07:36.455
has a feel that is excellent.

00:07:36.522 --> 00:07:38.991
I can literally use
it with one hand.

00:07:39.058 --> 00:07:40.992
The edge-- still sharp.

00:07:41.059 --> 00:07:41.727
Nicely done.

00:07:41.794 --> 00:07:43.995
 Thank you.

00:07:44.096 --> 00:07:45.565
[music playing]

00:07:45.631 --> 00:07:48.301
 All right, bladesmiths, to
see how sharp your weapons are,

00:07:48.401 --> 00:07:51.570
I will try to cut
through these pineapples.

00:07:51.637 --> 00:07:52.738
James, you're up first.

00:07:52.805 --> 00:07:53.773
You ready for this?
- Let's go.

00:07:53.839 --> 00:07:54.540
DOUG MARCAIDA: Let's do this.

00:07:54.607 --> 00:07:58.144
[music playing]

00:08:07.286 --> 00:08:07.920
 (WHISPERING) Nice.

00:08:08.020 --> 00:08:08.621
 Nice job.

00:08:08.721 --> 00:08:09.488
 (WHISPERING) Thanks.

00:08:09.555 --> 00:08:11.123
 All right, James--

00:08:11.190 --> 00:08:12.691
just a little off the top.

00:08:12.791 --> 00:08:15.194
Your edge is sharp,
cuts cleanly all the way

00:08:15.261 --> 00:08:16.895
through these pineapples.

00:08:16.962 --> 00:08:17.930
It will cut.

00:08:18.030 --> 00:08:18.764
 Thank you.

00:08:18.864 --> 00:08:19.798
 All right, Paul, your turn.

00:08:19.865 --> 00:08:20.332
Ready?

00:08:20.399 --> 00:08:21.433
 Yep.

00:08:21.534 --> 00:08:25.104
[music playing]

00:08:36.048 --> 00:08:36.782
 There you go, man.

00:08:36.882 --> 00:08:37.917
 Gosh.

00:08:37.984 --> 00:08:38.918
[music playing]

00:08:38.984 --> 00:08:40.920
 All right, Paul,
it is razor sharp.

00:08:40.986 --> 00:08:42.688
Just the thinness
of your metal here

00:08:42.788 --> 00:08:44.590
cuts through, no resistance.

00:08:44.657 --> 00:08:45.824
If you look at the
pineapple heads,

00:08:45.924 --> 00:08:47.459
they're all still
standing right there.

00:08:47.526 --> 00:08:48.594
It's very sharp.

00:08:48.694 --> 00:08:50.963
And more importantly,
it will cut.

00:08:51.063 --> 00:08:52.330
 Thank you.

00:08:52.431 --> 00:08:53.899
[music playing]

00:08:53.999 --> 00:08:57.169
 James, Paul, you've both done
an incredible amount of work.

00:08:57.236 --> 00:08:59.305
However, there can only
be one "Forged in Fire"

00:08:59.371 --> 00:09:01.106
champion in this competition.

00:09:01.173 --> 00:09:02.542
And that champion is--

00:09:06.912 --> 00:09:08.180
Paul.

00:09:08.246 --> 00:09:10.349
Congratulations, you're the
new "Forged in Fire" champion.

00:09:10.449 --> 00:09:14.019
James, please surrender
your gun chai.

00:09:14.119 --> 00:09:16.055
JAMES: Well, I'm pretty
happy I've made it this far.

00:09:16.121 --> 00:09:18.324
I don't think I could be too
disappointed in what I've done,

00:09:18.391 --> 00:09:19.858
considering how the
weapon performed.

00:09:19.925 --> 00:09:21.259
My blade was just
a little too heavy.

00:09:21.359 --> 00:09:22.260
Congratulations.
- Great.

00:09:22.327 --> 00:09:23.129
 You deserve it, buddy.

00:09:23.229 --> 00:09:24.596
 Good job.

00:09:24.696 --> 00:09:26.231
JAMES: It's been a
really great experience.

00:09:26.298 --> 00:09:27.800
I did the best I could.

00:09:27.900 --> 00:09:29.502
No matter what you do in life,
there's going to be challenges.

00:09:29.602 --> 00:09:31.603
And you're not going
to always succeed.

00:09:31.703 --> 00:09:33.573
Just get back up, get
back on the horse.

00:09:36.042 --> 00:09:37.009
[music playing]

00:09:37.109 --> 00:09:38.277
WIL WILLIS: Paul,
congratulations, you're

00:09:38.343 --> 00:09:39.812
the "Forged in Fire" champion.

00:09:39.912 --> 00:09:42.547
And that is a title that comes
with a check for $10,000.

00:09:42.647 --> 00:09:44.282
Good job, brother.

00:09:44.349 --> 00:09:46.452
 Thank you, thank you.

00:09:46.552 --> 00:09:47.920
I just couldn't be happier.

00:09:47.986 --> 00:09:49.621
This is, like-- got to be
the craziest thing that's

00:09:49.721 --> 00:09:51.223
ever happened to me so far.

00:09:51.289 --> 00:09:54.359
I mean, I know I'm only 19,
but I still can't believe it.

00:09:54.460 --> 00:09:55.728
I'm the "Forged
in Fire" champion,

00:09:55.828 --> 00:09:56.662
and it feels incredible.

00:09:56.729 --> 00:10:00.266
[music playing]

